    "['no synchronization', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'no synchronization;', 'parent_command': ['set protocols bgp local-as [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set protocols bgp local-as [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nno synchronization;\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, the equivalent BGP synchronization setting is controlled by the `synchronization` statement under `routing-options`. However, since Cisco's `no synchronization` is the default behavior in Juniper (Juniper doesn't synchronize IGP and BGP by default), this command would typically be omitted in Juniper configurations. The above translation shows how it would appear if explicitly configured, though it's usually unnecessary.\", 'trans_template': 'no synchronization;'}]]": 1,
